COURSE.push({
id: 'm12', short: 'Final project', title: 'Final project: test an online bank', minutes: 120,
lead: 'Put everything together on a real public demo: page objects, a clean set-up through the API, tests that check the page and the server, and a pipeline.',
learn: ['plan a small test project from scenarios to a pipeline', 'build page objects for a real site that has no labels', 'combine an API set-up, a UI action and an API check in one test', 'work politely with a public, rate-limited demo service'],
body: `
<h2>The project</h2>
<p>You will test <a href="https://parabank.parasoft.com/parabank/index.htm" target="_blank" rel="noopener">ParaBank</a>, a demo online bank that its makers publish for practising testing. It has customers, accounts, transfers and a REST API. You will write a small but real test project with three tests, and everything from this course goes into it: locators, actions, web-first assertions, isolation, page objects, unique data, the API and a CI pipeline.</p>
${co('Be a polite guest', 'ParaBank is a shared public service, and it limits how many requests one visitor can make (the answer is then "429 Too Many Requests"). Do not run the whole suite again and again in a row. Register one customer for a group of tests, not one for every test, and wait a few minutes if you see a 429. Never type real personal data into it: use made-up values. It is also a demo, so it may be reset or be down: try again later before you blame your code.', true)}
<h2>The three tests</h2>
${tbl(['#', 'Scenario', 'What it proves'], [
  ['1', '<b>Register a new customer</b> through the page with a unique user name, see the welcome message, and open the accounts overview, where at least one account is listed', 'The registration flow works end to end'],
  ['2', '<b>Mismatched passwords are rejected</b>: fill the form with two different passwords, submit it, and see the message "Passwords did not match." while staying on the registration page', 'The form validates its input'],
  ['3', '<b>A transfer changes both balances</b>: a customer with two accounts transfers 50.00 in the page. Both balances change by 50.00 in the accounts overview <b>and</b> on the server (checked through the API)', 'What the page shows is what the server has']
])}
<h2>What makes this site a good exercise</h2>
<ul><li><b>The registration form has no labels.</b> Fields cannot be found with <code>get_by_label</code>. Their ids contain dots (<code>customer.firstName</code>), so <code>#customer.firstName</code> would not work as a CSS selector. The fallback is an attribute selector: <code>[id="customer.firstName"]</code>. This is the honest use of "CSS as the last resort": when the page offers nothing better, say so in a comment.</li><li><b>The page updates by itself.</b> Parts of the accounts overview are filled in after the page loads, so you rely on web-first assertions, never on a sleep.</li><li><b>Data is shared and long-lived.</b> Other visitors use the same server, so balances are never "what you expect". You compare <b>before and after</b> instead of using fixed numbers.</li><li><b>The API base address has a path.</b> Remember the trap from module 9: end the base address with a slash and leave out the leading slash of the paths.</li></ul>
<h2>The structure to build</h2>
<pre class="mono-box">${L('pages/parabank_pages.py      LoginPage, RegisterPage, AccountsPage, TransferPage\ntests/test_parabank_project.py  the fixtures and the three tests\nrequirements.txt\npytest.ini\n.github/workflows/tests.yml\nREADME.md', 'src/test/kotlin/course/ParabankPages.kt        LoginPage, RegisterPage, AccountsPage, TransferPage\nsrc/test/kotlin/course/ParabankProjectTest.kt   the set-up and the three tests\nbuild.gradle.kts\n.github/workflows/tests.yml\nREADME.md')}</pre>
<h2>Step by step: build it</h2>
${steps('m12', [
  { do: 'Write the three scenarios as short manual test cases in your own words: title, steps, expected result.', why: 'You automate a test case, not a hunch. Writing them down first also gives you the checklist for the end, and a README for free.', see: 'Three short test cases, each with a clear expected result.' },
  { do: 'Open the three pages in a normal browser (registration, accounts overview, transfer funds) and note down how you would find each element. Use codegen to compare.', code: sh({ py: 'playwright codegen https://parabank.parasoft.com/parabank/register.htm', kt: './gradlew playwright --args="codegen https://parabank.parasoft.com/parabank/register.htm"' }), why: 'Looking before coding is cheaper than debugging later. Notice which elements have a role and a name, and which have only an id.', see: 'A list of locators for each page, with a note where you had to use an id.' },
  { do: 'Create the page objects: one class for the login page, one for registration, one for the accounts overview and one for the transfer page. Put the locators and the actions in them, and no assertions.', why: 'The knowledge of the pages lives in one place (module 7). If the site changes, you edit one file.', see: 'Four small classes. Run the tests later to see them in use.' },
  { do: 'Write the set-up: a customer registered once for the group of tests, through the API, with a unique user name. Also write a helper that reads the balance of an account from the API.', why: 'The API is the quick door for data (module 9), and one registration per group respects the rate limit. A unique name keeps runs from colliding (module 8).', see: 'A customer with a known user name and id, and a function that returns a balance.' },
  { do: 'Write test 1, the registration, and run it.', why: 'Start with the simplest flow, and see it green before adding more. Check the welcome message and the accounts overview with web-first assertions.', see: 'One green test.' },
  { do: 'Write test 2, the mismatched passwords, and run it.', why: 'A negative test proves that the page refuses what it should refuse. The message is found by its text, a user-facing locator.', see: 'Two green tests.' },
  { do: 'Write test 3, the transfer: create a second account through the API, read both balances, sign in through the page, transfer 50.00, and check both balances in the overview and through the API.', why: 'This is the test that matters most: a page that says "Transfer Complete" proves nothing until the server agrees. Comparing before and after makes it independent of other visitors.', see: 'Three green tests.' },
  { do: 'Run the whole project once with a visible browser, then make one test fail on purpose and open the trace.', why: 'You know your project works when you have seen both a pass and a failure that you understand (module 10). Run it only once or twice in a row, because of the rate limit.', see: 'A trace of a deliberate failure.' },
  { do: 'Add the CI workflow from module 11, and a README with: what the project tests, how to install, how to run, how to read a failure, and a link to the CI run.', why: 'A project that others can install and run in five minutes is a real project. It is also what an employer or a teammate looks at first.', see: 'A green CI run and a README that a newcomer can follow.' },
  { do: 'Now compare your work with the reference solution below. Do not copy it: look for differences, and ask yourself which version is clearer.', why: 'There is no single correct solution. The comparison is where you learn what you would do differently.', see: 'A short list of things you would change in your own project.' }
])}
<h2>A reference solution</h2>
<p>This version was run against the live demo with the versions from module 2. Open it after you have built your own.</p>
<details><summary>Show the reference: page objects</summary>${code({ py: "from decimal import Decimal\n\nfrom playwright.sync_api import Page\n\nSITE_URL = \"https://parabank.parasoft.com/parabank\"\n\n\ndef money(value: Decimal) -> str:\n    \"\"\"Format an amount the way ParaBank shows it, for example $365.50.\"\"\"\n    return f\"${value:,.2f}\"\n\n\nclass LoginPage:\n    def __init__(self, page: Page):\n        self.page = page\n        self.username = page.locator('input[name=\"username\"]')\n        self.password = page.locator('input[name=\"password\"]')\n        self.log_in = page.get_by_role(\"button\", name=\"Log In\")\n        self.error = page.locator(\"p.error\")\n\n    def open(self) -> None:\n        self.page.goto(f\"{SITE_URL}/index.htm\")\n\n    def sign_in(self, username: str, password: str) -> None:\n        self.username.fill(username)\n        self.password.fill(password)\n        self.log_in.click()\n\n\nclass RegisterPage:\n    def __init__(self, page: Page):\n        self.page = page\n        self.panel = page.locator(\"#rightPanel\")\n        self.register_button = page.get_by_role(\"button\", name=\"Register\")\n\n    def open(self) -> None:\n        self.page.goto(f\"{SITE_URL}/register.htm\")\n\n    def fill_form(self, fields: dict[str, str]) -> None:\n        for field_id, value in fields.items():\n            # the form has no labels, and the ids contain dots, so an attribute selector is used\n            self.page.locator(f'[id=\"{field_id}\"]').fill(value)\n\n    def submit(self) -> None:\n        self.register_button.click()\n\n\nclass AccountsPage:\n    def __init__(self, page: Page):\n        self.page = page\n        self.heading = page.get_by_role(\"heading\", name=\"Accounts Overview\")\n        self.rows = page.locator(\"#accountTable tbody tr\")\n\n    def open(self) -> None:\n        self.page.get_by_role(\"link\", name=\"Accounts Overview\").click()\n\n    def row(self, account_id: int):\n        return self.rows.filter(has_text=str(account_id))\n\n\nclass TransferPage:\n    def __init__(self, page: Page):\n        self.page = page\n        self.amount = page.locator(\"#amount\")\n        self.from_account = page.locator(\"#fromAccountId\")\n        self.to_account = page.locator(\"#toAccountId\")\n        self.transfer_button = page.get_by_role(\"button\", name=\"Transfer\")\n        self.result = page.locator(\"#showResult\")\n\n    def open(self) -> None:\n        self.page.get_by_role(\"link\", name=\"Transfer Funds\").click()\n\n    def transfer(self, amount: Decimal, from_id: int, to_id: int) -> None:\n        self.amount.fill(str(amount))\n        self.from_account.select_option(str(from_id))\n        self.to_account.select_option(str(to_id))\n        self.transfer_button.click()", kt: "package course\n\nimport com.microsoft.playwright.Locator\nimport com.microsoft.playwright.Page\nimport com.microsoft.playwright.options.AriaRole\nimport java.math.BigDecimal\nimport java.util.Locale\n\nconst val SITE_URL = \"https://parabank.parasoft.com/parabank\"\n\n/** Formats an amount the way ParaBank shows it, for example $365.50. */\nfun money(value: BigDecimal): String = \"$\" + String.format(Locale.US, \"%,.2f\", value)\n\nclass LoginPage(private val page: Page) {\n    val username: Locator = page.locator(\"input[name=\\\"username\\\"]\")\n    val password: Locator = page.locator(\"input[name=\\\"password\\\"]\")\n    val logIn: Locator = page.getByRole(AriaRole.BUTTON, Page.GetByRoleOptions().setName(\"Log In\"))\n\n    fun open() {\n        page.navigate(\"$SITE_URL/index.htm\")\n    }\n\n    fun signIn(user: String, pass: String) {\n        username.fill(user)\n        password.fill(pass)\n        logIn.click()\n    }\n}\n\nclass RegisterPage(private val page: Page) {\n    val panel: Locator = page.locator(\"#rightPanel\")\n    val registerButton: Locator = page.getByRole(AriaRole.BUTTON, Page.GetByRoleOptions().setName(\"Register\"))\n\n    fun open() {\n        page.navigate(\"$SITE_URL/register.htm\")\n    }\n\n    fun fillForm(fields: Map<String, String>) {\n        for ((fieldId, value) in fields) {\n            // the form has no labels, and the ids contain dots, so an attribute selector is used\n            page.locator(\"[id=\\\"$fieldId\\\"]\").fill(value)\n        }\n    }\n\n    fun submit() {\n        registerButton.click()\n    }\n}\n\nclass AccountsPage(private val page: Page) {\n    val heading: Locator = page.getByRole(AriaRole.HEADING, Page.GetByRoleOptions().setName(\"Accounts Overview\"))\n    val rows: Locator = page.locator(\"#accountTable tbody tr\")\n\n    fun open() {\n        page.getByRole(AriaRole.LINK, Page.GetByRoleOptions().setName(\"Accounts Overview\")).click()\n    }\n\n    fun row(accountId: Int): Locator = rows.filter(Locator.FilterOptions().setHasText(accountId.toString()))\n}\n\nclass TransferPage(private val page: Page) {\n    val amount: Locator = page.locator(\"#amount\")\n    val fromAccount: Locator = page.locator(\"#fromAccountId\")\n    val toAccount: Locator = page.locator(\"#toAccountId\")\n    val transferButton: Locator = page.getByRole(AriaRole.BUTTON, Page.GetByRoleOptions().setName(\"Transfer\"))\n    val result: Locator = page.locator(\"#showResult\")\n\n    fun open() {\n        page.getByRole(AriaRole.LINK, Page.GetByRoleOptions().setName(\"Transfer Funds\")).click()\n    }\n\n    fun transfer(value: BigDecimal, fromId: Int, toId: Int) {\n        amount.fill(value.toPlainString())\n        fromAccount.selectOption(fromId.toString())\n        toAccount.selectOption(toId.toString())\n        transferButton.click()\n    }\n}", file: { py: 'pages/parabank_pages.py', kt: 'src/test/kotlin/course/ParabankPages.kt' }, ex: 'pb-pages' })}</details>
<details><summary>Show the reference: set-up and tests</summary>${code({ py: "import json\nimport re\nimport uuid\nfrom decimal import Decimal\n\nimport pytest\nfrom playwright.sync_api import APIRequestContext, Page, Playwright, expect\n\nfrom pages.parabank_pages import (\n    SITE_URL,\n    AccountsPage,\n    LoginPage,\n    RegisterPage,\n    TransferPage,\n    money,\n)\n\nJSON = {\"Accept\": \"application/json\"}\nPASSWORD = \"Passw0rd\"\n\n\ndef registration_fields(username: str) -> dict[str, str]:\n    return {\n        \"customer.firstName\": \"Test\",\n        \"customer.lastName\": \"User\",\n        \"customer.address.street\": \"1 Test Street\",\n        \"customer.address.city\": \"Testville\",\n        \"customer.address.state\": \"TS\",\n        \"customer.address.zipCode\": \"12345\",\n        \"customer.phoneNumber\": \"5550100\",\n        \"customer.ssn\": \"123-45-6789\",\n        \"customer.username\": username,\n        \"customer.password\": PASSWORD,\n        \"repeatedPassword\": PASSWORD,\n    }\n\n\n@pytest.fixture(scope=\"module\")\ndef api(playwright: Playwright):\n    context = playwright.request.new_context(base_url=SITE_URL + \"/\")\n    yield context\n    context.dispose()\n\n\n@pytest.fixture(scope=\"module\")\ndef customer(api: APIRequestContext) -> dict:\n    \"\"\"Register one customer through the form endpoint. The public demo limits requests.\"\"\"\n    username = f\"qa_{uuid.uuid4().hex[:12]}\"\n    api.get(\"register.htm\")\n    response = api.post(\"register.htm\", form=registration_fields(username))\n    assert \"Your account was created successfully\" in response.text()\n\n    login = api.get(f\"services/bank/login/{username}/{PASSWORD}\", headers=JSON)\n    expect(login).to_be_ok()\n    return {\"username\": username, \"id\": login.json()[\"id\"]}\n\n\ndef balance_of(api: APIRequestContext, account_id: int) -> Decimal:\n    response = api.get(f\"services/bank/accounts/{account_id}\", headers=JSON)\n    expect(response).to_be_ok()\n    return json.loads(response.text(), parse_float=Decimal)[\"balance\"]\n\n\ndef test_registers_a_new_user(page: Page):\n    register = RegisterPage(page)\n    username = f\"qa_{uuid.uuid4().hex[:12]}\"\n    register.open()\n    register.fill_form(registration_fields(username))\n    register.submit()\n\n    expect(register.panel).to_contain_text(f\"Welcome {username}\")\n    expect(register.panel).to_contain_text(\"Your account was created successfully\")\n\n    accounts = AccountsPage(page)\n    accounts.open()\n    expect(accounts.heading).to_be_visible()\n    expect(accounts.rows.first).to_be_visible()\n\n\ndef test_mismatched_passwords_are_rejected(page: Page):\n    register = RegisterPage(page)\n    fields = registration_fields(f\"qa_{uuid.uuid4().hex[:12]}\")\n    fields[\"repeatedPassword\"] = \"Different1\"\n    register.open()\n    register.fill_form(fields)\n    register.submit()\n\n    expect(page.get_by_text(\"Passwords did not match.\")).to_be_visible()\n    expect(page).to_have_url(re.compile(\"/register.htm\"))\n\n\ndef test_transfer_changes_both_balances(page: Page, api: APIRequestContext, customer: dict):\n    accounts = api.get(f\"services/bank/customers/{customer['id']}/accounts\", headers=JSON).json()\n    account_a = accounts[0][\"id\"]\n    created = api.post(\n        \"services/bank/createAccount\",\n        params={\"customerId\": customer[\"id\"], \"newAccountType\": 1, \"fromAccountId\": account_a},\n        headers=JSON,\n    )\n    expect(created).to_be_ok()\n    account_b = created.json()[\"id\"]\n    before_a, before_b = balance_of(api, account_a), balance_of(api, account_b)\n    amount = Decimal(\"50.00\")\n\n    login = LoginPage(page)\n    login.open()\n    login.sign_in(customer[\"username\"], PASSWORD)\n    transfer = TransferPage(page)\n    transfer.open()\n    transfer.transfer(amount, account_a, account_b)\n\n    expect(transfer.result).to_contain_text(\"Transfer Complete!\")\n\n    overview = AccountsPage(page)\n    overview.open()\n    expect(overview.row(account_a)).to_contain_text(money(before_a - amount))\n    expect(overview.row(account_b)).to_contain_text(money(before_b + amount))\n\n    assert balance_of(api, account_a) == before_a - amount\n    assert balance_of(api, account_b) == before_b + amount", kt: "package course\n\nimport com.google.gson.JsonParser\nimport com.microsoft.playwright.APIRequest\nimport com.microsoft.playwright.APIRequestContext\nimport com.microsoft.playwright.assertions.PlaywrightAssertions.assertThat\nimport com.microsoft.playwright.options.FormData\nimport com.microsoft.playwright.options.RequestOptions\nimport org.junit.jupiter.api.AfterAll\nimport org.junit.jupiter.api.Assertions.assertEquals\nimport org.junit.jupiter.api.Assertions.assertTrue\nimport org.junit.jupiter.api.BeforeAll\nimport org.junit.jupiter.api.Test\nimport java.math.BigDecimal\nimport java.util.UUID\nimport java.util.regex.Pattern\n\nclass ParabankProjectTest : BaseTest() {\n    private val password = \"Passw0rd\"\n    private lateinit var api: APIRequestContext\n    private lateinit var username: String\n    private var customerId = 0\n\n    private fun registrationFields(user: String): Map<String, String> = mapOf(\n        \"customer.firstName\" to \"Test\",\n        \"customer.lastName\" to \"User\",\n        \"customer.address.street\" to \"1 Test Street\",\n        \"customer.address.city\" to \"Testville\",\n        \"customer.address.state\" to \"TS\",\n        \"customer.address.zipCode\" to \"12345\",\n        \"customer.phoneNumber\" to \"5550100\",\n        \"customer.ssn\" to \"123-45-6789\",\n        \"customer.username\" to user,\n        \"customer.password\" to password,\n        \"repeatedPassword\" to password,\n    )\n\n    private fun uniqueUsername() = \"qa_\" + UUID.randomUUID().toString().replace(\"-\", \"\").take(12)\n\n    private fun json(): RequestOptions = RequestOptions.create().setHeader(\"Accept\", \"application/json\")\n\n    @BeforeAll\n    fun registerCustomer() {\n        // One customer for the whole class, because the public demo limits requests.\n        api = playwright.request().newContext(APIRequest.NewContextOptions().setBaseURL(\"$SITE_URL/\"))\n        username = uniqueUsername()\n        val form = FormData.create()\n        registrationFields(username).forEach { (key, value) -> form.set(key, value) }\n        api.get(\"register.htm\")\n        val response = api.post(\"register.htm\", RequestOptions.create().setForm(form))\n        assertTrue(response.text().contains(\"Your account was created successfully\"))\n\n        val login = api.get(\"services/bank/login/$username/$password\", json())\n        assertThat(login).isOK()\n        customerId = JsonParser.parseString(login.text()).asJsonObject[\"id\"].asInt\n    }\n\n    @AfterAll\n    fun closeApi() {\n        api.dispose()\n    }\n\n    private fun balanceOf(accountId: Int): BigDecimal {\n        val response = api.get(\"services/bank/accounts/$accountId\", json())\n        assertThat(response).isOK()\n        return JsonParser.parseString(response.text()).asJsonObject[\"balance\"].asBigDecimal\n    }\n\n    @Test\n    fun registersANewUser() {\n        val register = RegisterPage(page)\n        val user = uniqueUsername()\n        register.open()\n        register.fillForm(registrationFields(user))\n        register.submit()\n\n        assertThat(register.panel).containsText(\"Welcome $user\")\n        assertThat(register.panel).containsText(\"Your account was created successfully\")\n\n        val accounts = AccountsPage(page)\n        accounts.open()\n        assertThat(accounts.heading).isVisible()\n        assertThat(accounts.rows.first()).isVisible()\n    }\n\n    @Test\n    fun mismatchedPasswordsAreRejected() {\n        val register = RegisterPage(page)\n        val fields = registrationFields(uniqueUsername()).toMutableMap()\n        fields[\"repeatedPassword\"] = \"Different1\"\n        register.open()\n        register.fillForm(fields)\n        register.submit()\n\n        assertThat(page.getByText(\"Passwords did not match.\")).isVisible()\n        assertThat(page).hasURL(Pattern.compile(\"/register.htm\"))\n    }\n\n    @Test\n    fun transferChangesBothBalances() {\n        val accounts = JsonParser.parseString(\n            api.get(\"services/bank/customers/$customerId/accounts\", json()).text()\n        ).asJsonArray\n        val accountA = accounts[0].asJsonObject[\"id\"].asInt\n        val created = api.post(\n            \"services/bank/createAccount\",\n            json()\n                .setQueryParam(\"customerId\", customerId)\n                .setQueryParam(\"newAccountType\", 1)\n                .setQueryParam(\"fromAccountId\", accountA)\n        )\n        assertThat(created).isOK()\n        val accountB = JsonParser.parseString(created.text()).asJsonObject[\"id\"].asInt\n        val beforeA = balanceOf(accountA)\n        val beforeB = balanceOf(accountB)\n        val amount = BigDecimal(\"50.00\")\n\n        val login = LoginPage(page)\n        login.open()\n        login.signIn(username, password)\n        val transfer = TransferPage(page)\n        transfer.open()\n        transfer.transfer(amount, accountA, accountB)\n\n        assertThat(transfer.result).containsText(\"Transfer Complete!\")\n\n        val overview = AccountsPage(page)\n        overview.open()\n        assertThat(overview.row(accountA)).containsText(money(beforeA - amount))\n        assertThat(overview.row(accountB)).containsText(money(beforeB + amount))\n\n        assertEquals(0, (beforeA - amount).compareTo(balanceOf(accountA)))\n        assertEquals(0, (beforeB + amount).compareTo(balanceOf(accountB)))\n    }\n}", file: { py: 'tests/test_parabank_project.py', kt: 'src/test/kotlin/course/ParabankProjectTest.kt' }, ex: 'pb-tests' })}</details>
<h2>Where to go next</h2>
<ul><li><b>Visual and accessibility checks</b>: screenshot comparisons and an accessibility scanner for pages.</li><li><b>Component and contract tests</b>: test a piece of the interface, or the API contract, without the whole system.</li><li><b>Richer reports</b>: Allure or a similar tool, with history and trends of flaky tests.</li><li><b>Test environments in containers</b>: run the application and the tests together on a clean machine.</li><li><b>Reading other people's tests</b>: open the test folders of open-source projects, and compare their structure with yours.</li></ul>
<p>When you are ready, take the final exam, and go through the interview flashcards out loud.</p>
`,
takeaways: ['A project starts from scenarios, and the scenarios become the README.', 'When a page offers no role, label or text, an id attribute selector is an honest last resort. Say why in a comment.', 'Set up data through the API, act in the page, and check in the page and on the server.', 'Compare before and after instead of expecting fixed numbers on shared data.', 'A project that others can install, run and understand in minutes is part of the work.'],
quiz: [
  { q: 'The registration form has no labels, and its field ids contain dots. What is the best locator?', o: ['An attribute selector for the id, with a comment that explains why', 'get_by_label, which always works', 'nth(3) on all inputs', 'A fixed sleep and a tab key'], a: 0, why: 'When no user-facing locator exists, an id is stable. The dots mean that #id would not work, so the attribute form [id="customer.firstName"] is used.' },
  { q: 'Why compare balances before and after a transfer instead of expecting fixed numbers?', o: ['The demo data is shared and long-lived, so the starting balance is not known in advance', 'Playwright cannot compare numbers', 'Fixed numbers are slower', 'The page hides balances'], a: 0, why: 'A test that depends on a number it does not control breaks when anything else changes it.' },
  { q: 'Why is the customer created through the API in this project?', o: ['It is fast, and it keeps the number of page-driven requests low on a rate-limited service', 'Because forms cannot be tested', 'Because the API is never wrong', 'Because pages cannot register users'], a: 0, why: 'Use the page for what you test (registration in test 1), and the quick door for set-up.' },
  { type: 'multi', q: 'Which of these belong in the README of the project?', o: ['What the project tests', 'How to install and run it', 'How to read a failure and open a trace', 'A link to the CI run', 'The real password of a person'], a: [0, 1, 2, 3], why: 'A README lets a newcomer succeed. Secrets and personal data never belong in a repository.' },
  { q: 'The demo answers 429 Too Many Requests. What do you do?', o: ['Wait a few minutes, run fewer times, and register once per group of tests', 'Add more parallel workers', 'Add retries until it works', 'Remove all assertions'], a: 0, why: 'More requests would only make it worse. Be a polite guest of a shared service.' },
  { type: 'order', q: 'Put the building of the project in order.', items: ['Write the scenarios as manual test cases', 'Build the page objects', 'Write the set-up and the helper for the API', 'Write the tests one by one, running each', 'Add the pipeline and the README'], why: 'Plan, structure, set-up, tests, then the packaging that makes it usable by others.' }
],
practice: { id: 'p-m12', title: 'Your project, and its self-review',
  brief: '<p>Build the project, and then review it against the list below. Be strict: for every line, write <b>yes</b>, <b>no</b>, or <b>partly</b>, and for every "no" or "partly" write what you would do about it.</p>',
  template: '1. Three scenarios written as manual test cases:\n2. Page objects, no assertions in them:\n3. Unique data, set-up through the API:\n4. No sleeps, only actions and web-first assertions:\n5. Tests independent and passing alone:\n6. Balances compared before and after:\n7. A trace opened for a deliberate failure:\n8. A green CI run with artifacts:\n9. A README that a newcomer can follow:\n10. What I would improve next:\n',
  checks: ['Every locator is user-facing, or has a comment that explains why not', 'No test uses a sleep or a plain assertion on a value read once', 'Each test can run alone and in any order', 'Data is unique, and no secret is in the repository', 'The pipeline is green and keeps the evidence of a failure', 'The README tells a newcomer how to install, run and read a failure'],
  model: '<p><b>What a strong project looks like:</b> three small tests with clear names; four page objects with business-named actions; one fixture that creates a customer through the API; before-and-after balance checks in the page and on the server; no sleeps; a CI workflow that uploads traces; a README with a "how to read a failure" section.</p><p><b>Good ideas for the next step:</b> add a test of the login page and a test of opening a new savings account; share the registration through a stored state; run the suite with two browsers; add a visual check of the accounts overview; and write down in the README which tests are the smoke set.</p>' }
});
